<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.9.1: Evaluating Expressions for Different Values of x</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01404</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.9.1: Evaluating Expressions for Different Values of x</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0804f787-7589-44d1-adcc-d288a70772eb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">Lin and Diego are discussing two expressions: <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
<para id="para-00002">Lin says, “I think the two expressions are equivalent.”</para>
<para id="para-00003">Diego says, “I think the two expressions are only equal for some values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.”</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00004">Do you agree with either of them? Explain or show your reasoning.</para>
  
  </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00005">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00006">I agree with Diego. Sample explanation: If we find the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> for different values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, say 0, 1, 2, 3, and 4, we can see that they are not always equal. As the table shows, they are only equal sometimes, for example, when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is 2 and 4.</para>
    

    
<table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable" id="table-00001">
  <tgroup cols="3"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
    <entry>
      1
    </entry>
    <entry>
      1
    </entry>
    <entry>
      2
    </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
        <entry>
          2
        </entry>
        <entry>
          4
        </entry>
        <entry>
          4
        </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry>
            3
          </entry>
          <entry>
            9
          </entry>
          <entry>
            8
          </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              16
            </entry>
            <entry>
              16
            </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                5
              </entry>
              <entry>
                25
              </entry>
              <entry>
                32
              </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                  10
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  100
                </entry>
                <entry>
                  1,024
                </entry>
                </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>
</solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
